olour 1 on a 0 background. In every output the frames are unchanged and only their insides get filled. The fill colour depends only on the size of the empty interior:\n\n| Interior side | Fill colour |\n|---|---|\n| 1×1 | 7 |\n| 2×2 | 2 |\n| 3×3 | 7 |\n| 4×4 | 2 |\n| 5×5 | 7 |\n| 6×6 | 2 |\n\nChecking this against the pairs:\n- Pair 1 has interiors of 1, 2 and 3. They become 7, 2 and 7.\n- Pair 2 has interiors of 1 → 7 and 4 → 2.\n- Pair 3 has interiors of 3, 2, 4, 5 and 6. They become 7, 2, 2, 7 and 2.\n- Pair 4 has interiors of 5 → 7 and 4 → 2.\n- Pair 5 has interiors of 2, 1 and 3. They become 2, 7 and 7.\n\nSo the rule is: **an odd interior side gives 7, and an even side gives 2.** Nothing else in the grid changes.\n\n**Construction.** For each frame object:\n1. Take its bounding box.\n2. The interior is the box shrunk by one cell on every side.\n3. Paint the background cells of that interior with 7 if its width is odd, or 2 if it is even.\n\nEach frame is one stage, so there is one emit per frame and a final emit at the end.\n\n**Test input.** It has four frames:\n- A 10×10 frame at (7,10). Its interior is 8×8, so it gets 2.\n- An 8×8 frame at (2,1). Its interior is 6×6, so it gets 2.\n- A 7×7 frame at (11,1). Its interior is 5×5, so it gets 7.\n- A 5×5 frame at (0,12). Its interior is 3×3, so it gets 7.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        iy0, ix0, iy1, ix1 = y0 + 1, x0 + 1, y1 - 1, x1 - 1\n        if iy1 < iy0 or ix1 < ix0:\n            continue\n        w = ix1 - ix0 + 1\n        col = 7 if w % 2 == 1 else 2\n        sub = g[iy0:iy1 + 1, ix0:ix1 + 1]\n        sub[sub == bg] = col\n        emit(g, f\"Filled the {iy1-iy0+1}x{w} interior of the frame at ({y0},{x0}) with {col} because its side is {'odd' if col == 7 else 'even'}.\")\n    emit(g, \"All frame interiors filled: odd-sized with 7, even-sized with 2.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The fill colour depends only on the size of the empty interior:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"| Interior side | Fill colour |"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"So the rule is: **an odd interior side gives 7, and an even side gives 2.** Nothing else in the grid changes."}],"count":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"All frame interiors filled: odd-sized with 7, even-sized with 2."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Take its bounding box."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"5b6062e80af6c5858abe35a1f3a91741f906dd0a3258bb97b1aa86171e30bdfe","task_sha256":"c4bf443e9b39534feb0bd26c1ffbaab24671b41de320dac70ae19532518bc008","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
